# Cloudflare Workers assets ignore
# GitHub still tracks everything normally — this only affects what CF uploads.

# Raw shelf photos (large HEIC files, multi-GB total)
Floors/

# JSON source (already baked into index.html)
biomed-shelf-ranges.json

# Build tooling
.build_locator.py
*.py

# Instruction docs
Instructions.txt
SHELF-MAPPING-INSTRUCTIONS.md
CATALOG.md

# Test corpus + harness (saved SRU responses; the app never reads these at runtime)
fixtures/
Tools/

# Git internals (CF was choking on the 991 MB pack file)
.git/

# Local tooling state. "assets.directory" is the repo root, so anything not listed here is
# served publicly — .wrangler/cache/wrangler-account.json carries the account id and the
# account's email address, and both of these once shipped by accident. Not credentials
# (the OAuth token lives outside the repo), but not for publication either.
.wrangler/
.claude/
.gitattributes
.assetsignore

# Source, not site
ios/
README.md

# Misc downloads that ended up in the repo
*.exe
*.zip
*.msix
*.xz
*.tar
# Scans and other documents that landed here — the app serves index.html, not paperwork,
# and "assets.directory" is the repo root, so anything not listed here is published.
*.pdf
